// v2.89.0 (group B) — the `.axon` input `socket_served.rs` never
// had on disk.
//
// Same precisely-small gap as the v2.67.0 gates: this one already deploys through
// the real `POST /v1/deploy` and boots a real TCP listener, so it was always a
// path proof. What it lacked is a program on disk, so nothing could catch the
// citation going stale.
//
// v2.67.0's finding is worth restating, because it is why this file exists at
// all: the OSS server had NO WebSocket route — not a stub, none — while the
// public README led with "session-typed WebSocket dialogue as a first-class
// primitive". And when a route did appear, every socket got a hardcoded
// canonical chat schema, so an adopter could declare a protocol and be served
// something else.
//
// The protocol below is exact duals: the broker receives an Order and sends a
// Fill; the client does the reverse. `socket Wire` carries it, and the served
// schema must be THIS one.

type Order { sku: String }

type Fill { id: String }

session Trade {
    broker: [ receive Order, send Fill, end ]
    client: [ send Order, receive Fill, end ]
}

socket Wire { protocol: Trade }
